ode (source)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/state.json" "file_sha256" "b604e3cf3d1bb5fd9774f1ad83835d7bda57d58ad3023b5a271ef3b40f64451c"} {"question" "q-333640" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "an unstable node (source)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/state.json" "file_sha256" "b604e3cf3d1bb5fd9774f1ad83835d7bda57d58ad3023b5a271ef3b40f64451c"} {"question" "q-333643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }2]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n$y=-x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/state.json" "file_sha256" "b604e3cf3d1bb5fd9774f1ad83835d7bda57d58ad3023b5a271ef3b40f64451c"} {"question" "q-333643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-2x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-2x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/450d43a4cbf6dad8d54edbb66fc4a6e44e491290e1dc5d1303057fb0eb7928a7.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/state.json" "file_sha256" "b604e3cf3d1bb5fd9774f1ad83835d7bda57d58ad3023b5a271ef3b40f64451c"} {"question" "q-333643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b20be943601aa019f404b7f365efd0336dcd5697c2bf0e37d0e29a3fef87be38"} {"question" "q-333643" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/state.json" "file_sha256" "b604e3cf3d1bb5fd9774f1ad83835d7bda57d58ad3023b5a271ef3b40f64451c"} {"question" "q-333643" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "a stable"] ["text" "an unstable"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathaca